From: robyroro <41092915+robyroro@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 08:31:43 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?=EF=BB=BFtheme:=20take=20the=20product=20icons?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20from=20//ghost/branding/theme?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Points the browser's, the installers' and the updater's icons, the Start
tiles, and the product logos packed for the UI and WebUI at the files
tools/brand_icons.py generates in //ghost/branding/theme, on Windows.
Other platforms keep Chromium's. The incognito and app-list icons stay
upstream's: they carry no product logo.

grit looks a scaled image up as default_<scale>_percent/<file>, so one
path can't name three scales: each scale has its own branch on the
output context.

Why: Chromium picks its icons by branding_path_component and names them directly in .rc files, with no argument for another brand.
Upstream: not upstreamable: product-specific branding
Signed-off-by: robyroro <41092915+robyroro@users.noreply.github.com>

